{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 88","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_88&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A six dimensional \"cube\" (a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cube) has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> vertices at the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd5133409bfab44596a526c1d90afe6b9f6f652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 3,\\pm 3,\\pm 3,\\pm 3,\\pm 3,\\pm 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" />. This <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cube has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea78c80fcbdf9fce3229b511584d34de2f11047c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$192\\text{ 1-D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> edges and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e946dea05208da925ed0ac480889263352b73d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240\\text{ 2-D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> edges. This <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cube gets cut into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd4047d17f6a27e50bac31e17483cfcc34242eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6=46656$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> smaller congruent \"unit\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cubes that are kept together in the tightly packaged form of the original <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cube so that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/9986c8dd48a4e9d065c387de405742ed3d00c817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46656$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> smaller <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cubes share <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/3196c671aecf98ceb14026b8616856502cf978d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-D$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> square faces with neighbors (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c167e7be1298f1c7c9d38beaf293d171c22d2e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{one}$\" width=\"26\" height=\"7\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-D square face shared by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed31a4938f13d32ca55dc463512816fff68a681a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{several}$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> unit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cube neighbors). How many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-D squares are faces of one or more of the unit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-cubes?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_88&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Any 2-dimensional face of any of the unit hypercubes lies in one of the 2-dimensional axis-parallel planes that we get by choosing four of the six coordinates and holding them constant. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdbbadbe78a9e78de62083129a1c2b8ebb16ad86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{4} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"81\" height=\"55\" /> ways to choose the four coordinates and 7 choices (anything from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) to choose for each, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e34e762dfc69d866a029958c2f12efcab40c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 7^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> planes. Once we've fixed this plane we're reduced to the 2-dimensional problem of counting unit squares in a square grid of edge-length 6. But of course there are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> of these. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1591107c91d760fd505135c6c3cebc8e0e51bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 7^4 \\cdot 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>More generally, one can show that the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />-dimensional <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53fe11dd0742443dcce2817257972d9b495c9cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times \\cdots \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> faces in a division of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-dimensional cube of edge-length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is precisely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36daa863075b6598046c892501db7d7c65ac6285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{m} \\cdot (k + 1)^{n - m} \\cdot k^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"182\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>~ Imported from solution by JBL\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_88&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_87\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 87\">Problem 87</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_89\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 89\">Problem 89</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</